  "sources": [
    "KB sfx-ambience law 4: music and ambience occupy different geometries",
    "Late tail and reflections from the room geometry (Eyring), scripts/spatial_hrtf/room.py; absorption coefficients from presets/materials/room_materials.json (concrete stands in for cut stone: a hard, reflective surface; nearest material there)",
    "Chirped echo and stepped-pyramid acoustics: https://www.nature.com/news/2004/041213/full/news041213-5.html",
    "Maya palace rooms: the corbel vault needed very heavy walls and gave narrow interior spaces; rooms were finished with limestone plaster (https://www.webpages.uidaho.edu/arch499/nonwest/mayan/architecture.htm, https://www.ancient-history-sites.com/?p=140142); the Cancuen palace is described as hundreds of small rooms with 20-foot corbel-arched ceilings (https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2000/09/000909224023.htm). Search-result text only; pages not opened.",
    "ESTIMATE: widths of 2.5-9 m, lengths of 9-30 m and heights of 5-10 m are written from \"narrow\" and \"about 20 feet\" and are not a survey of a real building; plaster stands in for limestone plaster in room_materials.json; no acoustic measurement of a Maya palace was found"
  ]
